Artificial Intelligence (AI): The broad science of mimicking human intelligence and problem-solving capabilities in machines so they can perform tasks autonomously or semi-autonomously.
​Machine Learning (ML): A subset of AI focused on building applications that learn from data and improve their accuracy over time without being explicitly programmed for every scenario.
​Deep Learning (DL): A specialized subset of ML powered by multi-layered artificial neural networks (hence "deep") designed to process vast amounts of complex, unstructured data like images, audio, and text.[ Artificial Intelligence (AI) ]
